{"ambiguity_notes":["The compiled flag is supplied packet metadata; no compiler was invoked to independently establish it.","The literal conclusion does not separately list 0<Z_s, probability-measure status, a pointwise Radon–Nikodym density identity, or Integrable(q_s log(q_s),γ). The reconstruction retains the actual listed conclusions without adding these as separate assertions.","The displayed witness uniqueness concerns the stationary equation for every z. A separate minimizer or mean characterization is not a stated conclusion.","The declared packet_sha256 is retained as packet metadata; the exact raw-byte and LF-normalized hashes are independently checked against the lease."],"decoder_context_used":{"compiler_started":false,"definition_context":"Only the five approved-definition-context entries in packet0.json and its neutral Lean statement.","inputs_read":["lease.json","packet0.json"],"repository_or_history_context_used":false,"source_fidelity_verdict_produced":false,"source_text_visible":false,"web_used":false},"hidden_assumptions":["No additional public mathematical assumptions are present beyond the displayed typeclass, regularity, curvature, measurability and strict-positivity hypotheses. Normalization and integrability certificates are not input binders."],"mathematical_reconstruction":"Let E be a complete finite-dimensional real Hilbert space, equipped with its Borel structure and canonical volume, and let S be an arbitrary measurable space. Dimension zero is permitted. Let V:E→ℝ be C² and κ≥1, with\n  (1/κ)‖v‖² ≤ D²V(x)[v,v] ≤ ‖v‖²\nfor all x,v∈E. Let η:S→ℝ and y:S→E be measurable, with η(s)>0 for every s.\nThere exists a measurable p:S→E such that, for every s,\n  p(s)+η(s)∇V(p(s))=y(s),\nand every z∈E satisfying z+η(s)∇V(z)=y(s) equals p(s).\nUsing this same p throughout, define\n  ρ_s(u)=V(p(s)+√η(s) u)−V(p(s))−√η(s)⟨∇V(p(s)),u⟩,\n  μ=volume.tilted(x↦−V(x)),\n  R_s=μ.tilted(x↦−‖x−y(s)‖²/(2η(s))),\n  r_s=(x↦(√η(s))⁻¹(x−p(s)))_* R_s,\n  γ=the centered covariance-identity Gaussian on E,\n  Z_s=∫exp(−ρ_s(u))dγ(u),\n  q_s(u)=exp(−ρ_s(u))/Z_s.\nHere each tilt is the normalized exponential tilt when its exponential weight is integrable, and the zero measure otherwise. For every s, r_s is absolutely continuous with respect to γ, and its canonical extended-nonnegative-real KL divergence from γ is finite. Its canonical log-likelihood representative llr(r_s,γ) and ρ_s are integrable with respect to r_s. The identity llr(r_s,γ)(u)=log(q_s(u)) holds r_s-almost everywhere. Furthermore,\n  KL(r_s‖γ).toReal = ∫q_s(u)log(q_s(u))dγ(u)\n                   = −∫ρ_s(u)dr_s(u)−log(Z_s).\nThe statement supplies p internally, places no upper bound on positive η, and requires no separately supplied stationary selector, probability, normalization, integrability or entropy certificate. The almost-everywhere identity does not assert pointwise equality of the chosen log-likelihood representative.","raw_input_binding":{"bytes":4440,"declared_packet_sha256":"9c4839d6d07eee8a1a4d83ddcbca49032191453213684038d36897ef225480e2","input_binding_verified":true,"lf_sha256":"d23f48238c6672747bc2002e6d44343bf809e44f0d2f8634a00f5f9033285982","packet_id":"ASTIS-BLIND-7a3fabb04f0008c3","packet_path":".astis/decoder-33/packet0.json","raw_sha256":"b9bc34586ea6116189c59d17bf17c467fdf133a68f8b7657ca830a7d822c5e66","statement_sha256":"7a3fabb04f0008c3b3075843c4815dfe2c2f982c73ed32f893cbdbdf0e383a32"},"semantic_slots":{"assumptions":"κ≥1; V is C² in the real Fréchet sense; for every x,v∈E, κ⁻¹‖v‖²≤D²V(x)[v,v]≤‖v‖²; η and y are measurable; η(s)>0 for all s. The gradient is the Hilbert Riesz representative and D²V is the actual iterated Fréchet derivative. There are no public assumptions supplying a stationary selector, normalization, a probability law, partition-function finiteness, integrability, means, entropy, or comparison certificates.","conclusion":"The measurable p exists and is the unique solution at each s. For each s, r_s≪γ; KL(r_s‖γ)≠∞; llr(r_s,γ) is genuinely integrable under r_s; llr(r_s,γ)(u)=log(q_s(u)) for r_s-almost every u; ρ_s is genuinely integrable under r_s; KL(r_s‖γ).toReal=∫q_s(u)log(q_s(u))dγ(u); and KL(r_s‖γ).toReal=−∫ρ_s(u)dr_s(u)−log(Z_s).","constants":"The Hessian bounds are exactly 1/κ and 1; κ≥1. The quadratic tilt contains exactly 2η_s in its denominator. Centering/scaling uses exactly √η_s and its inverse. γ has covariance identity. Z_s is the Gaussian integral ∫exp(−ρ_s)dγ, with no extra Lebesgue or Gaussian normalization multiplier inserted. Every positive η_s is permitted; there is no step-size upper bound or additional dimension-dependent constant.","domains":"E is any complete finite-dimensional real Hilbert space with its Borel measurable structure and canonical volume, including dimension zero. S is any measurable carrier. V, κ, η, y and all formulas take real values where indicated; p_s,x,z,u,v lie in E. KL is valued in extended nonnegative reals, while KL.toReal and the displayed integrals and logarithms are real-valued.","objects":"A potential V:E→ℝ, condition parameter κ, measurable parameter functions η:S→ℝ and y:S→E, and an internally produced measurable stationary solution p:S→E. Define ρ_s(u)=V(p_s+√η_s u)−V(p_s)−√η_s⟨∇V(p_s),u⟩; μ=volume tilted by −V; R_s=μ tilted by −‖x−y_s‖²/(2η_s); r_s is the pushforward of R_s by x↦(√η_s)⁻¹(x−p_s); γ is the centered covariance-identity Gaussian; Z_s=∫exp(−ρ_s)dγ and q_s(u)=exp(−ρ_s(u))/Z_s. Tilts are normalized exponential tilts when integrable, and zero measures otherwise.","quantifiers":"For every such E and S, every V and κ satisfying the global hypotheses, and every measurable η and y with η(s)>0 for every s, there exists one measurable function p. For every s, p_s solves p_s+η_s∇V(p_s)=y_s; for every s and every z∈E satisfying z+η_s∇V(z)=y_s, z=p_s. The same p defines every downstream measure and function, and all subsequent conclusions hold for every s.","scope_sense":"All stationary equations, Hessian bounds and witness uniqueness statements are pointwise in their displayed variables. The likelihood-representative equality is only almost everywhere under r_s, not a pointwise identity or an equality only under γ. The relative-entropy finiteness is an explicit extended-real claim, distinct from its real-valued .toReal identities. Both entropy identities use the same literal r_s, γ, ρ_s and Z_s produced from the same p. The pushforward is the actual measure map, and integrability is genuine Bochner integrability."}}